WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.194
Today is November 04, 2026.

3
00:00:07.194 --> 00:00:12.697
Overnight, Wall Street drifted higher on light volume as midterm ballots were cast.

4
00:00:12.697 --> 00:00:18.775
The S and P 500 added about 28 points, or 0.36 percent.

5
00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:24.743
The Nasdaq Composite gained about 208 points, or 0.83 percent.

6
00:00:24.743 --> 00:00:28.505
This was a technical bounce, not a change in trend.

7
00:00:28.505 --> 00:00:33.677
Blue-chip defensives held firm, and Berkshire Hathaway closed at a record high.

8
00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:36.116
The bigger story is rates.

9
00:00:36.116 --> 00:00:41.275
Markets now see a 78.9 percent chance of a December rate hike.

10
00:00:41.275 --> 00:00:46.336
Tariffs, war, and AI spending are all pushing inflation higher.

11
00:00:46.336 --> 00:00:51.875
Big tech is selling debt faster, and that extra supply is pushing Treasury yields up.

12
00:00:51.875 --> 00:00:56.643
Higher rates for longer put heavy pressure on growth stock valuations.

13
00:00:56.643 --> 00:00:58.885
Jobs are not the problem.

14
00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:04.437
September job openings rose to 7.52 million, and layoffs fell.

15
00:01:04.437 --> 00:01:11.054
Friday's payrolls are expected at 59 thousand, with unemployment steady at 4.2 percent.

16
00:01:11.054 --> 00:01:14.694
On the election, the bulls and bears disagree.

17
00:01:14.694 --> 00:01:18.015
Markets expect Democrats to win the House.

18
00:01:18.015 --> 00:01:20.993
Control of the Senate is still a toss-up.

19
00:01:20.993 --> 00:01:23.138
Bulls point to history.

20
00:01:23.138 --> 00:01:28.469
Since 1950, the S and P has risen in the year after every midterm.

21
00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:32.010
The average gain was 15.4 percent.

22
00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:37.010
UBS adds that light hedge fund positioning sets up a post-election rally.

23
00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:42.292
Bears point out that the index was already up 10.7 percent through October.

24
00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:46.630
In a typical midterm year, it is up about one percent by then.

25
00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:52.770
Morgan Stanley's Michael Wilson sees another nine percent drop, toward 7,100.

26
00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:57.966
He blames politics, worries about AI spending, and tighter liquidity.

27
00:01:57.966 --> 00:02:01.508
Then he sees a rebound to 8,000 next year.

28
00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:07.366
Citi reports large new short positions in S and P and Nasdaq futures last week.

29
00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:09.498
Here are the key levels.

30
00:02:09.498 --> 00:02:14.939
The S and P has closed below its half-year moving average for three straight sessions.

31
00:02:14.939 --> 00:02:18.763
Strong support sits near 7,200.

32
00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:23.015
The Nasdaq 100 bounced off its one-year moving average.

33
00:02:23.015 --> 00:02:27.648
Old support at 28,900 is now firm resistance.

34
00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:32.182
For the Nasdaq Composite, support is near 25,000.

35
00:02:32.182 --> 00:02:34.804
The VIX is still above 20.

36
00:02:34.804 --> 00:02:39.584
The CNN Fear and Greed Index slipped from 23 to 19.

37
00:02:39.584 --> 00:02:45.123
Once the election results are in, hedges get unwound, and swings could get bigger.

38
00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:50.037
If a Democratic sweep triggers a selloff, that could be a buying opportunity.

39
00:02:50.037 --> 00:02:53.125
Geopolitics is the main wild card.

40
00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:57.317
Washington and Tehran are reviewing a new proposal from Qatar.

41
00:02:57.317 --> 00:03:01.165
Qatar expects responses within 36 hours.

42
00:03:01.165 --> 00:03:06.520
Israel's Prime Minister Netanyahu is urging a strike on Iran right after the election.

43
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.934
The ceasefire is fragile.

44
00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:15.037
The United States hit targets near Qeshm Island, and Iran shot down two American drones.

45
00:03:15.037 --> 00:03:22.917
On the other side, Russia, Ukraine, and the United States will hold peace talks in Abu Dhabi on November 10 and 11.

46
00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:25.552
That news is weighing on oil.

47
00:03:25.552 --> 00:03:29.988
If crude starts climbing again, stocks face a new headwind.

48
00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:32.807
Tight money is hitting tech the hardest.

49
00:03:32.807 --> 00:03:39.057
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index rose 2.63 percent but faded off its highs.

50
00:03:39.057 --> 00:03:42.415
It is still below its one-year moving average.

51
00:03:42.415 --> 00:03:49.768
In October, the chip index fell 15.4 percent, and Q-Q-Q fell 6.7 percent.

52
00:03:49.768 --> 00:03:55.013
Morgan Stanley's tech momentum factor is down about 62 percent from its peak.

53
00:03:55.013 --> 00:04:00.576
That is deeper than the roughly 50 percent drop when the dot-com bubble burst in 2000.

54
00:04:00.576 --> 00:04:02.795
Earnings are not the problem.

55
00:04:02.795 --> 00:04:07.451
About 80 percent of reporting S and P companies have beaten estimates.

56
00:04:07.451 --> 00:04:09.804
The problem is the payback.

57
00:04:09.804 --> 00:04:13.603
Downstream AI users are earning big profits.

58
00:04:13.603 --> 00:04:16.875
Upstream builders are borrowing to keep spending.

59
00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:20.344
The market has stopped asking whether there is demand.

60
00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:24.265
It now asks whether all this spending will ever pay off.

61
00:04:24.265 --> 00:04:28.322
For the chip index, 10,000 is the line to watch.

62
00:04:28.322 --> 00:04:33.812
It is a round number, the one-year average, and a key Fibonacci retracement level.

63
00:04:33.812 --> 00:04:38.603
If AI stocks recover from there, the broader market can stabilize.

64
00:04:38.603 --> 00:04:43.309
If that level breaks, nothing else is big enough to lead the market higher.

65
00:04:43.309 --> 00:04:48.652
Big money is waiting for two things, the election result and the Anthropic IPO.

66
00:04:48.652 --> 00:04:56.422
Anthropic's buyers are pushing to cut its valuation from two trillion dollars to between 1.5 and 1.6 trillion.

67
00:04:56.422 --> 00:05:01.998
The roadshow could start next week, with a listing targeted for the week of November 16.

68
00:05:02.096 --> 00:05:05.759
AI infrastructure names are showing some strength.

69
00:05:05.709 --> 00:05:10.096
Fabrinet jumped after its fourteenth straight quarter of revenue growth.

70
00:05:10.096 --> 00:05:14.998
Goldman Sachs raised its forecasts for data center capacity and spending.

71
00:05:14.998 --> 00:05:23.331
Cipher Mining rose 18.4 percent after extending its leases to 20 years, worth about 9.1 billion dollars.

72
00:05:23.331 --> 00:05:28.503
Memory chip stocks got a lift after Apple said memory prices will keep rising.

73
00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:30.844
But their rebound was weak.

74
00:05:30.844 --> 00:05:37.473
The rush into defensive names like Coca-Cola, Eli Lilly, and Walmart was driven by fear of tech.

75
00:05:37.473 --> 00:05:39.704
It is not true safety.

76
00:05:39.704 --> 00:05:44.361
If tech bottoms, money will leave those stocks and flow back into tech.

77
00:05:44.361 --> 00:05:47.645
Three stocks have clear trade signals today.

78
00:05:47.645 --> 00:05:50.917
First, A-M-D is a conditional buy.

79
00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:56.959
Third-quarter revenue hit a record 13.4 billion dollars, up 45 percent.

80
00:05:56.959 --> 00:06:02.130
Earnings per share were 2.09 dollars, up 74 percent.

81
00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.799
Data center revenue nearly doubled to 8.5 billion dollars.

82
00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:13.711
Fourth-quarter guidance is 17 billion dollars, above the 16.3 billion Wall Street expected.

83
00:06:13.711 --> 00:06:17.045
Gross margin guidance is 55 percent.

84
00:06:17.045 --> 00:06:19.569
The weak spot is cash flow.

85
00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:24.998
Free cash flow fell 64 percent to 554 million dollars.

86
00:06:24.998 --> 00:06:28.147
Analysts had expected nearly two billion.

87
00:06:28.147 --> 00:06:32.094
The stock lost almost 200 dollars in a single month.

88
00:06:32.094 --> 00:06:36.309
It sits far below Lisa Su's 600 dollar ambition.

89
00:06:36.309 --> 00:06:40.782
Buy only if the after-hours gain holds through today's regular session.

90
00:06:40.782 --> 00:06:43.969
Exit if the stock gives back the whole gap.

91
00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:48.589
A drop in the chip index below 10,000 also means get out.

92
00:06:48.589 --> 00:06:52.853
If the move holds, it could lift chip stocks across the board.

93
00:06:52.853 --> 00:06:56.027
Second, Apple is a buy on dips.

94
00:06:56.027 --> 00:07:02.988
Fiscal-year revenue reached 478.8 billion dollars, up 15.1 percent.

95
00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:08.417
Net income rose 18 percent to 132.1 billion dollars.

96
00:07:08.417 --> 00:07:11.750
The stock gapped down on its margin guidance.

97
00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:21.174
December-quarter gross margin is guided at 45 to 46 percent, down from 47.9 percent, mainly because memory costs more.

98
00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:24.422
Every phone maker faces the same cost.

99
00:07:24.422 --> 00:07:28.270
Apple has the pricing power to pass it on to customers.

100
00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:33.466
The stock opened lower and closed higher, so sellers are running out of reasons.

101
00:07:33.466 --> 00:07:38.748
Its beta is 1.09, so it moves roughly in step with the market.

102
00:07:38.748 --> 00:07:43.772
Apple has historically filled every downside gap, and this gap is small.

103
00:07:43.772 --> 00:07:45.844
Buy into weakness.

104
00:07:45.844 --> 00:07:48.503
Take profits when the gap fills.

105
00:07:48.503 --> 00:07:51.763
Stop out on a close below Tuesday's low.

106
00:07:51.763 --> 00:07:56.493
Apple is usually the last big stock to fall in a Q-Q-Q pullback.

107
00:07:56.493 --> 00:08:00.157
When Apple falls, a bottom is often close.

108
00:08:00.157 --> 00:08:03.650
Third, Shopify is a sell into strength.

109
00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:10.194
Revenue was 3.74 billion dollars, up 32 percent, just missing estimates.

110
00:08:10.194 --> 00:08:14.140
Earnings per share were 49 cents, a slight beat.

111
00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:18.258
Free cash flow was 816 million dollars.

112
00:08:18.258 --> 00:08:23.687
But gross merchandise volume and gross profit grew less than big buyers had bet on.

113
00:08:23.687 --> 00:08:26.469
Holiday guidance was only in line.

114
00:08:26.469 --> 00:08:30.108
The stock trades near 96 times earnings.

115
00:08:30.108 --> 00:08:33.380
That is far richer than the top tech leaders.

116
00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:38.564
Shares fell more than 19 percent before the open and faded again in the afternoon.

117
00:08:38.564 --> 00:08:41.775
Use any relief bounce to cut positions.

118
00:08:41.775 --> 00:08:44.030
Do not buy into the drop.

119
00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.407
Here is what to watch next.

120
00:08:46.407 --> 00:08:49.140
The midterm results come out today.

121
00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:54.201
Qatar expects answers from Washington and Tehran within 36 hours.

122
00:08:54.201 --> 00:08:58.111
Watch whether A-M-D holds its gain in regular trading.

123
00:08:58.111 --> 00:09:00.905
October payrolls come out Friday.

124
00:09:00.905 --> 00:09:06.027
The Abu Dhabi peace talks are next week, followed by the Anthropic listing.

125
00:09:06.027 --> 00:09:09.446
The December Fed meeting decides the rate path.

126
00:09:09.446 --> 00:09:17.780
The levels to watch are 7,200 on the S and P, 25,000 on the Nasdaq, and 10,000 on the chip index.

127
00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.787
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

128
00:09:21.787 --> 00:09:25.954
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
